## What this changes

A form's calculations run in its calculation order (`/CO`), and a chain defined in the wrong order shows stale numbers without saying why. Acrobat has an order dialog (Prepare Form ▸ Set Field Calculation Order, with Up and Down).

**Prepare a form ▸ Calculation order**, an entry in the Fields tools that opens a page of its own in the panel, with a back arrow to Prepare a form:
- **a card that says whether the order is right.** When it isn't, an amber card says what is wrong in words: each field that calculates too early ("total calculates before sub, which it reads."), fields `/CO` leaves out (other viewers may not calculate them), and `/CO` entries that calculate nothing. It holds **Fix order**, which moves only what must move. When the order is right, a green card says so, with **Undo** after an order change;
- **a red card per loop** ("x and y read each other"): no order fixes a loop, so it links to the first field's formula (Field Properties ▸ Calculate) instead;
