A click beside the page, or in the gap between pages, left the selection as it was. Only Escape let go of it. That covers a selected comment, Edit's selected objects, the picture picked with the Select tool, and the text selection. Acrobat and other viewers deselect there.

The picked picture is the worst case: with a full-page scan, a click anywhere on the page picks the same picture again, so there was nowhere to click it away.

**Why.** Each page module lets go of its own selection on a click on its page's empty part. A press beside the pages begins on no page, so the router gives it to no page (`PagePress::Elsewhere` everywhere), and nothing let go.

**Change.**

- `PageRouter::began_off_the_pages()` says whether the press the pages hold began off every page.
- After the page loop, `document_area` calls `DocView::deselect_beside_pages()` on a primary **click** whose press began there **and** whose release lands off every page. That clears what Escape clears in each module:
  - the text selection and Select All of the document;
  - the picked picture;
  - the selected comment;
  - Edit's objects, through a new `ObjectSelection::deselect`, which is the `clear` that Escape uses;
  - the selected added item and link;
  - an Edit image selection, unless it is being cropped;
